WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.875
Canada's whistleblower laws are designed to fail.

00:00:02.875 --> 00:00:08.602
The International Bar Association ranks Canada's whistleblower protections among the worst in the developed world.

00:00:08.602 --> 00:00:11.352
The Canadian Forces are explicitly exempt.

00:00:11.352 --> 00:00:12.818
So are CSIS.

00:00:12.818 --> 00:00:14.204
So is CSE.

00:00:14.204 --> 00:00:15.027
Zero.

00:00:15.027 --> 00:00:20.647
That is the number of remedies ordered under the Public Servants Disclosure Protection Act in eighteen years of operation.

00:00:20.647 --> 00:00:27.465
The mandatory five-year review of the PSDPA, required by law since 2012, has never been conducted.

00:00:27.465 --> 00:00:32.590
The law that protects whistleblowers has never been reviewed to see if it actually protects whistleblowers.

00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:37.590
The burden of proof falls on the whistleblower — not on the employer — to prove reprisal intent.

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:42.909
In the United States, the Military Whistleblower Protection Act has existed since 1988.

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:46.943
In Canada, military personnel have no equivalent protection.

00:00:46.943 --> 00:00:47.795
None.

00:00:47.795 --> 00:00:51.840
Access to remedies is controlled by the Public Sector Integrity Commissioner.

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:55.363
In eighteen years, only seven referrals to the tribunal.

00:00:55.363 --> 00:00:56.227
Seven.

00:00:56.227 --> 00:00:58.374
The gatekeeper decides who gets through.

00:00:58.374 --> 00:01:00.022
And almost no one does.

00:01:00.022 --> 00:01:01.761
Section 504.

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:05.329
Twenty-nine counts filed in the Criminal Information — Form 2.

00:01:05.329 --> 00:01:09.159
Section 122, Breach of Trust by a Public Officer.

00:01:09.159 --> 00:01:12.590
Section 139, Obstruction of Justice.

00:01:12.590 --> 00:01:15.863
Section 380, Fraud over Five Thousand.

00:01:15.863 --> 00:01:17.830
These are not theoretical charges.

00:01:17.830 --> 00:01:21.477
These are documented offences sourced from the government's own records.

00:01:21.477 --> 00:01:27.534
Bill C-70 creates new foreign interference offences but zero whistleblower protections.

00:01:27.534 --> 00:01:36.272
The Magnitsky Act allows sanctions against foreign officials who commit human rights abuses — but there is no domestic equivalent for officials who abuse Canadians.

00:01:36.272 --> 00:01:37.590
The law is clear.

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:38.954
The tools exist.

00:01:38.954 --> 00:01:44.124
Section 504 of the Criminal Code gives every Canadian the right to file private prosecution.

00:01:44.124 --> 00:01:45.931
This page tells you how.
